# RUCHI — environment variables
# Copy to .env.local if you want to tune the AI layer or enable accounts.
# The app is fully functional with ZERO configuration: Puter.js handles AI
# in the browser (user-pays), and every AI capability has a deterministic
# fallback. Accounts need a Supabase project (below); without one the app
# stays fully usable in anonymous/local mode.

# ── AI provider ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# "puter" (default) — Puter.js gateway, no API keys, browser sign-in.
# "none"            — deterministic fallbacks only (offline testing).
# AI_PROVIDER=puter

# ── Models (must exist in Puter's catalog: https://docs.puter.com/AI/) ──
# Defaults: gpt-5-nano for both — image-capable, fast, cheapest input cost
# in Puter's OpenAI tier; ideal for photo analysis + short structured JSON.
# Try vision alternates: gpt-4o, gemini-2.5-flash, claude-sonnet-5.
# VISION_MODEL=gpt-5-nano
# TEXT_MODEL=gpt-5-nano

# ── RUCHI accounts (Supabase Auth + Postgres) ───────────────
# Supabase owns user identity, profiles, completed meals and cooking
# streaks behind row-level security. Puter is the AI layer ONLY — it is
# never used for RUCHI sign-in. Create a project at https://supabase.com,
# apply supabase/migrations/0001_ruchi_init.sql, then fill these in:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-publishable-anon-key
#
# ── Password reset ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Where reset-email links land. Must ALSO be allow-listed in the Supabase
# dashboard (Auth → URL Configuration → Redirect URLs). Leave unset for
# root deployments ("https://<origin>/" is used automatically); set it for
# non-root/preview deployments:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PASSWORD_RESET_REDIRECT=https://YOUR-DOMAIN/
